{"name":"Peppermint Pie","hex":"#aac7c1","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"peppermint","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A hybrid herb of the mint family (Mentha × piperita), formed by crossing watermint and spearmint, which has a high menthol content and a sharp flavor and is used in cooking, especially in herb teas and in confections. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","Any of various eucalypts of southeastern Australia whose leaves yield peppermint-like essential oils."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/peppermint"},{"term":"pie","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-3 language code for Piro."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A type of pastry that consists of an outer crust and a filling. (Savory pies are more popular in the UK and sweet pies are more popular in the US, so \"pie\" without qualification has different connotations in these dialects.)","Any of various other, non-pastry dishes that maintain the general concept of a shell with a filling."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pie"}],"entries":[{"title":"Peppermint","blocks":[{"text":"Peppermint is a hybrid species of mint, a cross between watermint and spearmint. Indigenous to Europe and the Middle East, the plant is now widely spread and cultivated in many regions of the world. It is occasionally found in the wild with its parent species."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/72/Pfefferminze_natur_peppermint.jpg/330px-Pfefferminze_natur_peppermint.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Peppermint","wikidata":"Q156037"},{"title":"Pie","blocks":[{"text":"A pie is a baked dish which is usually made of a pastry dough casing that contains a filling of various sweet or savoury ingredients. Sweet pies may be filled with fruit, nuts, fruit preserves, brown sugar, sweetened vegetables, or with thicker fillings based on eggs and dairy. Savoury pies may be filled with meat, eggs and cheese, or a mixture of meat and vegetables."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a6/Top_down_view_of_peach_pie_%28722379748%29.jpg/330px-Top_down_view_of_peach_pie_%28722379748%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pie","wikidata":"Q13360264"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0d/Mentha-piperita.JPG/500px-Mentha-piperita.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0d/Mentha-piperita.JPG/500px-Mentha-piperita.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Peppermint flowers","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMentha-piperita.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/49/Mentha_%C3%97_piperita_-_K%C3%B6hler%E2%80%93s_Medizinal-Pflanzen-095.jpg/330px-Mentha_%C3%97_piperita_-_K%C3%B6hler%E2%80%93s_Medizinal-Pflanzen-095.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/49/Mentha_%C3%97_piperita_-_K%C3%B6hler%E2%80%93s_Medizinal-Pflanzen-095.jpg/330px-Mentha_%C3%97_piperita_-_K%C3%B6hler%E2%80%93s_Medizinal-Pflanzen-095.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"An 1887 illustration from Köhlers; Medicinal Plants","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMentha_%C3%97_piperita_-_K%C3%B6hler%E2%80%93s_Medizinal-Pflanzen-095.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/94/From_%27Street_Life_in_London%27%2C_1877%2C_by_John_Thomson_and_Adolphe_Smith_%285780910909%29.jpg/500px-From_%27Street_Life_in_London%27%2C_1877%2C_by_John_Thomson_and_Adolphe_Smith_%285780910909%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, htt